          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Antoninus Pius</strong><br>\nAntoninus Pius was born as Titus Aurelius Fulvus Boionius Arrius Antoninus on September 19, 86 AD, in Lanuvium, near Rome. He came from a wealthy family and had a conventional education in rhetoric and law. His path to power began in the reign of Emperor Hadrian, under whom he held various political offices, gradually rising through the ranks of Roman society.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Adoption by Hadrian</strong><br>\nIn 138 AD, after a distinguished career in public service, Antoninus was adopted by Emperor Hadrian. This adoption was part of Hadrian's succession plan, which also included the adoption of Marcus Aurelius and Lucius Verus. Antoninus's adoption was a testament to his reputation for intelligence, integrity, and administrative ability.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Antoninus Pius as Emperor</strong><br>\nAntoninus Pius became emperor after Hadrian's death in 138 AD. His reign is marked by peace and stability, which earned him the title \"Pius\" after deifying his predecessor and honoring the Senate. He avoided unnecessary military campaigns and instead focused on administrative efficiency and the welfare of his subjects.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
