            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>His Governance and Administration</strong><br>\nAs an administrator, Antoninus Pius was known for his effective governance. He improved the legal system and financial administration of the empire. His reign saw the consolidation of Roman law and the enhancement of city infrastructures across the empire, including aqueducts, bridges, and public buildings.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Policies and Public Works</strong><br>\nAntoninus's economic policies were prudent and successful. He left the empire with a surplus in the treasury by controlling expenditures and promoting agricultural prosperity. He funded the construction and repair of public works, contributing to the economic and social stability of the Roman state.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Relationship with the Senate</strong><br>\nThroughout his reign, Antoninus maintained a harmonious relationship with the Roman Senate. He respected senatorial authority and sought its counsel, which was not common among other emperors. His cooperative approach with the Senate fostered a period of goodwill and relative lack of conflict in Roman politics.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
