          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Legal Reforms and Justice</strong><br>\nAntoninus Pius is also remembered for his legal reforms. He made significant changes to the Roman legal system, focusing on the humane treatment of slaves and the protection of orphans and minors. His enactments reflected his desire for fairness and justice for all his subjects, regardless of their social status.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural and Religious Contributions</strong><br>\nThe reign of Antoninus Pius was a time of cultural prosperity. He patronized the arts and literature and supported traditional Roman religious practices. Although Christianity was spreading, he did not pursue policies of religious persecution, allowing for a diversity of religious expressions to coexist in the empire.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Succession</strong><br>\nAntoninus Pius died on March 7, 161 AD, after a long and peaceful reign of 23 years. He was succeeded by Marcus Aurelius and Lucius Verus, whom he had groomed for the throne as part of Hadrian's long-term succession plan. His death was mourned throughout the empire, and he was deified by the Senate, solidifying his legacy as one of the good emperors of Rome.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
